// PolicyViolationState Severity of the violation findings — `fail` high, `warn` medium, `info` low.
type PolicyViolationState string

// PolicyCondition One test of a component. `value`'s type depends on the subject; a single
// string is accepted where a list is expected. Globs use `*` (any run,
// across `/`) and `?`, case-insensitive. A fact that is unknown (no
// license, no vulnerabilities, no package metadata) never matches — an
// unknown package is neither outdated nor up to date.
//
// | subject | operators | value |
// |---|---|---|
// | `severity` | `gte` | severity — the worst vulnerability of the component |
// | `vulnerability_id` | `is`, `matches` | ids / globs over advisory ids and CVEs |
// | `kev` | `is` | boolean — a vulnerability is on a KEV catalog (CISA, ENISA EUVD, VulnCheck) |
// | `kev_source` | `in` | catalog names (`cisa`, `enisa`, `vulncheck`) — one of them asserts a vulnerability is known-exploited |
// | `epss` | `gte` | number 0–1 — the highest EPSS |
// | `cwe` | `in` | CWE numbers |
// | `license` | `is`, `is_not` | SPDX id globs. `is` (deny): the expression can't be satisfied without a listed license — `MIT OR GPL-3.0-only` passes a GPL deny, `MIT AND GPL-3.0-only` doesn't; `WITH` is judged by its license. `is_not` (allow): it can't be satisfied by listed licenses alone. |
// | `license_group` | `in`, `not_in` | group refs — a group id or `category:<ScanCode category>` (e.g. `category:Copyleft`); same semantics as `is` / `is_not` |
// | `license_unresolved` | `is` | boolean — the license isn't a resolvable SPDX expression |
// | `outdated` | `is` | boolean — a newer stable release exists |
// | `versions_behind` | `gte` | integer ≥ 1 |
// | `age` | `gte` | days since this version was released |
// | `missing_hash` | `is` | `any` (no hash at all) or `strong` (no SHA-256-or-stronger) |
// | `integrity` | `is` | `mismatch` or `verified`: the SBOM hashes against the registry's published digests (unknown matches neither) |
// | `coordinates` | `matches`, `no_match` | `{group, name, version}` globs; `version` may be a range like `>=1.2.0, <2.0.0` |
// | `purl` | `matches`, `no_match` | purl globs |
// | `package_type` | `in`, `not_in` | purl types (`npm`, `maven`, …) |
// | `component.kind` | `in`, `not_in` | kinds: `software`, `model`, `dataset`, `ai-service` (the AI inventory) |
// | `model.supplier` | `in`, `not_in` | globs over a model's or AI service's supplier, manufacturer and publisher (a service's provider); `not_in` (allow list) holds when none of them is listed |
// | `model.name` | `matches`, `no_match` | globs over a model's or AI service's name and `group/name` (`meta-llama/Llama-2-*`); `no_match` (allow list) holds when neither is listed — "model not in the approved list" |
// | `model.license` | `is`, `is_not` | as `license`, for models and AI services only |
// | `model.task` | `in`, `not_in` | globs over the model card's task |
// | `dataset.name` | `matches`, `no_match` | globs over a dataset's name and the datasets a model card names; `no_match` holds when one of them isn't listed |
// | `expression` | `matches` | a [CEL](https://cel.dev) expression over `component` (`type`, `kind`, `group`, `name`, `version`, `purl`, `hashes`, `license.{raw,expression,ids,resolved}`), `vulns` (`count`, `ids`, `max_severity`, `max_severity_rank` 5–0, `kev`, `kev_sources`, `epss`, `cwes`), `pkg` (`known`, `latest`, `outdated`, `versions_behind`, `age_days`), `model` (`suppliers`, `task`, `architecture_family`, `datasets`) and `project` (`name`, `version`, `default_version`), e.g. `vulns.kev && pkg.versions_behind >= 3`. Unknown facts are null and never match; mistakes (syntax, misspelled field, non-boolean) are rejected when saving |
type PolicyCondition struct {
	Operator PolicyConditionOperator `json:"operator"`
	Subject  PolicyConditionSubject  `json:"subject"`

	// Value Per subject — see the table.
	Value interface{} `json:"value"`
}

// PolicyConditionOperator defines model for PolicyCondition.Operator.
type PolicyConditionOperator string

// PolicyConditionSubject defines model for PolicyCondition.Subject.
type PolicyConditionSubject string

