// GetIngestionHealth Is data still coming in?
//
// Problems with how findings arrive, across the projects you can see — computed
// live from each project's scan history (default versions; Xila's own advisory
// and policy runs are not watched):
//
//   - `stale` — a scanner that uploaded on a cadence (≥ 3 scans) has been silent
//     for more than 3× its usual gap (at least a day);
//   - `volume_drop` — the latest upload reported under half the findings of the
//     ones before (when those had ≥ 10): an expired token or a misconfigured
//     scanner usually looks like this, not like a clean project;
//   - `failed_scan` — the latest scan of a stream failed;
//   - `connector_failing` — a connector's last pull failed;
//   - `failed_jobs` — uploads that exhausted their ingest retries in 7 days.
//
// The leader checks hourly and sends `ingestion.anomaly` once per new problem.
//
// Corresponds with GET /ingestion-health (the `GetIngestionHealth` operationId).
