// UpdateFindingFieldsWithBodyWithResponse Edit a finding's title, severity or planned remediation date
//
// Editor. A `title` or `severity` set here overrides the scanner's and sticks: the
// next scan keeps it and triage-rule severity resets skip it, until `reset_title` /
// `reset_severity` hands the field back to the scanner (its value returns with the
// next scan). A severity change recomputes priority from every input (EPSS, KEV,
// exploits, reachability, exposure) and regroups duplicates; finding history names
// you. `planned_remediation_at` is the team's own target date (`null` clears it).
//
// Conflict detection: send `If-Match: "<updated_at>"` (as last read); if the finding
// changed since, the answer is `412` with the current finding and nothing is written.
