// McpWithBodyWithResponse MCP server for AI agents (Streamable HTTP, JSON-RPC 2.0)
//
// `MCP_ENABLED=true`; otherwise 404. The Model Context Protocol endpoint
// (revisions 2025-06-18, 2025-03-26, 2024-11-05): `initialize`, `ping`,
// `tools/list`, `tools/call`. A notification (no `id`) is answered `202`;
// batches are refused. Tools: `search_findings`, `get_finding`,
// `triage_finding`, `list_projects`, `get_fix_plan`,
// `list_remediation_actions`, `upload_scan`, `upload_sbom`, `generate_vex`,
// `get_gate_result`. Each runs as an API request with the caller's token, so
// the caller's role, a project-scoped token's confinement and the audit log
// apply unchanged (`changes.via = "mcp:<tool>"`). A refused or failed call is a
// tool result with `isError: true`, not a JSON-RPC error.
