// RunVulnmatchWithResponse Re-match stored SBOMs against the advisory sources now
//
// Instance admin. This is what keeps a stored SBOM **alive**: it matches every
// snapshot against the configured advisory sources (`VULNMATCH_SOURCES`: OSV.dev,
// GitHub Advisories, the local OSV mirror, private advisories — merged, one
// result per advisory) — recording each snapshot's matches, so old releases keep
// answering "was this vulnerable?" — and turns the current inventory's matches
// into findings (scanner `osv`), so a newly disclosed CVE appears with no
// re-scan and an upgraded dependency auto-closes. Runs after each SBOM upload
// and on a schedule (`VULNMATCH_INTERVAL`); this forces it.
//
// When some sources fail (`partial: true`), the healthy sources' matches are
// **added** but nothing is auto-closed and snapshot history is left as it was —
// a finding only the failed source knows must not be closed as fixed.
//
// Returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /vulnmatch (the `RunVulnmatch` operationId).
